From 1fff802335ca410fd75d1766b7d750f036a8763d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 09:12:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 35/39] gfx: BasicPlanarYCbCrImage::CopyData must not report
 failure under delayed conversion

BasicImageLayer::Paint swaps the BasicLayerManager's image factory into the
video ImageContainer for the duration of a paint. A decoder thread that calls
CreatePlanarYCbCrImage() inside that window gets a BasicPlanarYCbCrImage, and
VideoData::SetVideoDataToImage always requests delayed conversion before
CopyData(). CopyData copied the planes and then returned false, so
CreateAndCopyData returned null and the decoder reported
NS_ERROR_OUT_OF_MEMORY -> MEDIA_ERR_DECODE.

With OMTC off a software paint on the TouchPad takes 40-160 ms, so a decode
landed in the window within the first 10-60 frames of every clip.

Return the base copy's result, and true when conversion is delayed: the
image is fully usable, GetAsSourceSurface() converts on demand.
---
 gfx/layers/basic/BasicImages.cpp | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/gfx/layers/basic/BasicImages.cpp b/gfx/layers/basic/BasicImages.cpp
index fc1be6e9a1..4533f69c84 100644
--- a/gfx/layers/basic/BasicImages.cpp
+++ b/gfx/layers/basic/BasicImages.cpp
@@ -87,10 +87,17 @@ public:
 bool
 BasicPlanarYCbCrImage::CopyData(const Data& aData)
 {
-  RecyclingPlanarYCbCrImage::CopyData(aData);
+  if (!RecyclingPlanarYCbCrImage::CopyData(aData)) {
+    return false;
+  }
 
+  // The YCbCr copy above succeeded; delaying the RGB conversion is not a
+  // failure. GetAsSourceSurface() converts on demand when mDecodedBuffer is
+  // null. Returning false here made VideoData::CreateAndCopyData report OOM
+  // (MEDIA_ERR_DECODE) for any frame decoded while BasicImageLayer::Paint had
+  // swapped this factory into the video's ImageContainer.
   if (mDelayedConversion) {
-    return false;
+    return true;
   }
 
   // Do some sanity checks to prevent integer overflow
